 "text": "Hi. How I help you? Bears are naturally curious and attracted to food. need to reduce their interest, you can tie your food up high or in a locker and carry it at the same time. you want to attract bears to your camp? They' learn that your camp is a nice place to visit. If you see one at your camp, don't panic. Back away slowly. Don't turn your back on the bear, don't run, and don't make loud noises. Make sure you're not carrying any food. Bears are generally not interested in people, but they can become aggressive if they feel threatened. They' also looking for food and may see people as a source of food, so it's always best to be aware of your surroundings and to respect their space.",
